	(text "${TITLE}"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.34 7.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5.08 5.08)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0e7ab83d-d0dc-480c-988d-23d4e65a6368")
	)
	(text "Todo list:\n\n[] - Replace 5v buck-regulator with newer type\n[] - Devise a protection circuit so that a high voltage on USB will not\n	kill the 5v buck-regulator (see lighting-controller-8M [2.0.0]\n	- 2 ideal-diodes to mux the 5v?\n	- ideal diode from Vbus to Vin?\n	- Comparator to detect when VBus > 5V?\n	- Turn off USB load-switch (input) whenever 5V regulator is active?\n		- Be careful of the load switch (output)! Don't want that turning on if\n		output is higher! Software can check, but is that trustworthy enough?\n	- [BEST OPTION] Replace the 5V buck regulator with a buck-boost regulator!\n		- e.g. TPS63070 (4sw, ~ $0.50)\n			- 4th switch means it can block reverse voltages!\n			- Also means it can operate with a much lower voltage - 2.0V\n				- 3-4V when accounting for the input bridge rectifier\n\n[] - Replace 0603 0.1uF with 0402 version (already on board)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 2.54 215.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "12cc2192-359a-4f45-86af-05c6bb808517")
	)
	(text "~~ GPIO count ~~\nUnrestricted = 31\nSpecial = 6s (0, 45, 46, Tx, Rx)\nUnused if possible = 1u (26)\n\nGPIB = 16\n\nI2C-internal = 2s (Rx, Tx)\n- FUSB302 = 1s (45)\n- INT (TBD) = 1s (IO46)\n\nUSB-PD = 2\n\nSPI common = 3\n- Ethernet CS/INT/RST = 3\n- NOR flash (16MB) = 1\n\nTotal (remaining) = 25 + 4s (6 +2s)\n\n?? USB alt mode = 2-10\n?? Piicodev connector = 2 each\n?? 4pin JST connector = 2 each\n  "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.78 7.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1b320f3f-5098-48cb-9bda-b949c6c83e80")
	)
	(text "Some pins are used for bootstrapping, and thus\nthey must have the correct state when booting:\nGPIO- state - reason\n0   - FLOAT - Allows code to be downloaded\n46  - LOW/FLOAT - Download boot mode\n		- Only checked if 0 is LOW\n45  - LOW/FLOAT - Flash voltage\n		- Can be disabled using by an eFuse\n\nWeak pull-down on IO0, IO45, IO46 (strapping pins)\nWeak pull-up on IO43, IO44 (UART0 pins)\n\nADC1 (10 channels) available on GPIO's 1-10\nADC2 on GPIO's 11-18. Not available with WiFi\n\nNo DAC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2e82d361-3244-4ec6-a929-3fca344ead9e")
	)
	(text "For fast SPI, use GPIO's 9-14\nDefault SPI pins for FSPI:\nCS0 = 10\nSCK = 12\nMISO = 13\nMOSI = 35  ?\n(last one is strange. Hardware\nimplies it should be 11, but\nthe IDF uses 35...)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 73.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6b5b885b-86cf-4f57-a3ef-3528122d2519")
	)
